course: dictionary
lesson: 12780
title: Effervescence
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Effervescence is a noun. It means the bubbles of gas that rise in a liquid, like in fizzy drinks, and it can also mean lively, cheerful, bubbly energy. Both meanings come from the idea of bubbling up. «The effervescence in the glass rose in tiny silver bubbles.»
explain: In science, effervescence is a clue that a gas is being made. «When we mixed vinegar and bicarbonate of soda, the effervescence showed that a gas was forming.» If you see fizzing in a chemical reaction, ask yourself: is a gas being made?
explain: In stories, effervescence can describe a person's energy. «Her effervescence filled the room as she told us about her trip.» Here it does not mean bubbles at all. It means she was bursting with cheerful excitement. Use the context to choose the right meaning.
fact: Effervescence means bubbles of gas rising in a liquid, or lively, cheerful and excited behaviour.
fact: «Effervescence» comes from the idea of bubbling and fizzing.
fact: In science, effervescence shows that a gas is being made.
fact: «Effervescence» is an uncountable noun, so we say «some effervescence», not «an effervescence».
fact: Check the context: fizzing in a glass means bubbles, but a bubbly, happy person means lively energy.
exercise: What is effervescence in a fizzy drink? | *The bubbles of gas that rise in the liquid | The sticky sugar at the bottom | The sweet taste of the syrup | The cold ice cubes floating on top
exercise: «When Sam dropped the tablet in water, the effervescence made the glass fizz.» What causes the fizz? | Sam shaking the table | Cold ice cubes | The glass being made of plastic | *Gas bubbles rising as the tablet dissolves
exercise: Mia says, «Her effervescence lit up the whole party.» What does effervescence mean here? | A heavy coat | *Lively, cheerful, bubbly excitement | Angry shouting | Sleepy and quiet
test: In a science lesson, vinegar and bicarbonate of soda show effervescence. What does this tell you? | The mixture has turned into metal | The mixture has frozen solid | Nothing is happening at all | *A gas is being made
test: «The children were full of effervescence on the first day of the holidays.» Which word is closest in meaning to effervescence here? | *Excitement | Gloom | Tiredness | Silence
exam: Which sentence uses effervescence to mean bubbles of gas? | «Her effervescence made everyone smile.» | «The effervescence in the bottle rose to the top.» | *«The effervescence showed a gas was being made.» | «He had no effervescence at all today.»
